Also, you can use a pick-axe forever; you'll soon use up the
charges in a wand.

> Taking off all but one expendable piece of armor, wielding an
> expendable weapon, dropping all your scrolls and potions,
> picking up and reading one unknown scroll at a time, if you
> have sufficient HP to survive the possible results like a
> scroll of fire (thus why you drop scrolls and potions before
> reading each scroll) or a cursed scroll of teleportation,
> might teleport you elsewhere on the level to a part you
> haven't seen, or magic map the level for you, and in the
> process perhaps enchant a weapon or a bit of armor or destroy
